      textEn: 'I am a wanderer and mountain-climber, said he to his heart, I love not the plains, and it seemeth I cannot long sit still.And whatever may still overtake me as fate and experience\u2014a wandering will be therein, and a mountain-climbing: in the end one experienceth only oneself.',
      textPt: 'I am a wanderer and mountain-climber, said he to his heart, I love not the plains, and it seemeth I cannot long sit still.And whatever may still overtake me as fate and experience\u2014a wandering will be therein, and a mountain-climbing: in the end one experienceth only oneself.',
